 Ra 1.6 um lam 0.2 mm: slope 2.88 deg, halo ~1.41 deg (vs 0.53 sun)

== 6. Image shift with sun motion ==
sun moves ~15 deg/h (hour angle); image shifts ~ d*dalpha
d=1 m: shift 0.26 m/h; time to shift 1 blur (9 mm): 2.1 min
d=2 m: shift 0.52 m/h; time to shift 1 blur (19 mm): 2.1 min
d=3 m: shift 0.79 m/h; time to shift 1 blur (28 mm): 2.1 min

Deviation of tilted back surface (tilt 20 deg) vs incidence on front (thin-wedge model)
 inc 0: deflection -10.64 deg; relative to normal-incidence 0.0 deg
 inc 10: deflection -10.06 deg; relative to normal-incidence 0.58 deg
 inc 20: deflection -10.06 deg; relative to normal-incidence 0.58 deg
 inc 30: deflection -10.59 deg; relative to normal-incidence 0.05 deg
 inc 40: deflection -11.7 deg; relative to normal-incidence -1.07 deg
 inc 50: deflection -13.58 deg; relative to normal-incidence -2.94 deg
 inc 60: deflection -16.48 deg; relative to normal-incidence -5.84 deg
Rigid image shift = d*dalpha; extra distortion = change in deflection above (deg), e.g. 10 deg off-design -> 1 to 2 deg change, >sun disc

